      ],
      "text": "Execution model: ODT plans and governs; OCA-backed Codex or Cline sessions execute implementation against the target repository.\nLocal backend control plane: a lightweight Node.js context server handles intake updates, repo validation, uploads, ODT run requests, execution bundle creation, and agent launch status.\nHybrid prompting: OCI GenAI can optionally generate stage prompts; fallback prompts and reviewer overrides (custom prompt) keep the workflow resilient and customizable.\nGuardrails: 7 stage guided pipeline, prompt hardening, repo-aware impact analysis, Oracle accessibility guidance before delegation, and mandatory human approval before delivery.\nDecision points: human can refine scope, update prompts, request re-analysis, approve delegation, review changed files, and fill gaps before final approval.\nAutomation boundaries: ODT does not auto-merge, bypass human approval, or replace developer judgment.\nIntegration points: ODT/FEDIT dashboard, reports/odt artifacts, OCI GenAI, fallback prompt templates, local context server, OCA Codex/Cline, repo diff review.\n",
